Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-Pi space along which the
  pore fraction is preserved: simultaneously rescaling the
  dimensionless groups along g keeps the LPBF physics invariant.

  Generator 1:
    Pi⊥1 x exp(+0.538*eps), Pi⊥2 x exp(+0.335*eps), Pi⊥3 x exp(-0.460*eps), Pi⊥4 x exp(+0.127*eps), Pi⊥5 x exp(+0.550*eps), Pe_vap x exp(+0.056*eps), Pr x exp(+0.253*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi⊥5 while increase Pi⊥1, increase Pi⊥2, decrease Pi⊥3, increase Pi⊥4, increase Pe_vap, increase Pr
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 2:
    Pi⊥1 x exp(-0.692*eps), Pi⊥2 x exp(+0.436*eps), Pi⊥3 x exp(-0.393*eps), Pe_vap x exp(+0.379*eps), Pr x exp(+0.177*eps)
    Meaning: decrease Pi⊥1 while increase Pi⊥2, decrease Pi⊥3, increase Pe_vap, increase Pr
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 3:
    Pi⊥1 x exp(-0.343*eps), Pi⊥2 x exp(-0.658*eps), Pi⊥4 x exp(+0.234*eps), Pi⊥5 x exp(+0.520*eps), Pr x exp(+0.352*eps)
    Meaning: decrease Pi⊥2 while decrease Pi⊥1, increase Pi⊥4, increase Pi⊥5, increase Pr
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged


